                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Nit, this is going to catch all errors, and not print a stack trace when we hit an unexpected error (out of memory for example).\n\nMight be better to explicitly catch the error types we expect here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "scripts/validate_configs.py",
                    "line": 272,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I think I'm fine just taking this whole exception clause out if you want.  The only ones I can really think of are obscure things, like FileNotFoundError when reading the schema.  I don't think we really need explicit `expect_fail` support for all these, which is what this catch does, but if someone wants to add a new one in the future they can do it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "scripts/validate_configs.py",
                    "line": 272,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
